{
    "background_story": "Allison was a bright and curious child, but she struggled to grasp the concept of reading and writing. Born into a remote community with limited access to education, she had never seen a book or held a pencil before the age of six. When a team of volunteers arrived at her village to establish a school, Allison was fascinated by the strange symbols on the blackboard. Despite being considered preliterate, she was eager to learn. With the help of a patient teacher, Allison began to recognize letters and sounds, slowly but surely. As she progressed, her confidence grew, and she became one of the most enthusiastic students in the class. Allison's journey from preliterate to literate was a testament to the power of education and the human desire to learn and connect with the world.",
